  "headBody": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-GB\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Harbour redevelopment plan approved - Example News</title>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Example News\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Harbour redevelopment plan approved\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Council votes 9-4 for the waterfront scheme.\">\n</head><body>\n<div id=\"top-bar\" class=\"top-bar\"><a href=\"/\">Example News</a><ul class=\"main-nav\"><li><a href=\"/world\">World</a></li><li><a href=\"/business\">Business</a></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ad-slot advert\" data-ad=\"leaderboard\">Advertisement</div>\n<div class=\"layout\"><div class=\"story-column\">\n<article class=\"story\">\n<h1>Harbour redevelopment plan approved</h1>\n<div class=\"story-meta\"><span class=\"byline\">Jon Weaver</span> <span class=\"dateline\">12 June 2024</span></div>\n<figure class=\"lead-image\"><img src=\"/img/harbour.jpg\" alt=\"Cranes over the old harbour\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Cranes over the old harbour. Photograph: A. Reporter</figcaption></figure>\n<p class=\"lede\">Councillors voted 9-4 on Tuesday night to approve a 1.2bn waterfront scheme, ending three years of debate.</p>\n<p>The plan covers 40 hectares of former dock land and includes 3,500 homes, a new tram line and a public park along the river.</p>\n<p>Opponents argued the scheme would price out existing residents. \"We asked for a guarantee on affordable units and we did not get one,\" said councillor Priya Nair.</p>\n<div class=\"related-links\"><h4>Read more</h4><ul><li><a href=\"/a\">Tram line explained</a></li><li><a href=\"/b\">Dock history</a></li></ul></div>\n<p>Construction is expected to begin in 2026.</p>\n<div class=\"share-tools\"><button>Share</button><a href=\"#comments\">Comments (12)</a></div>\n</article>\n<div id=\"comments\" class=\"comments-section\"><h2>Comments</h2><div class=\"comment\"><span class=\"user\">sam</span><p>About time.</p></div></div>\n</div>\n<aside class=\"rail\"><div class=\"most-read\"><h3>Most read</h3><ol><li><a href=\"/1\">One</a></li><li><a href=\"/2\">Two</a></li><li><a href=\"/3\">Three</a></li></ol></div><div class=\"ad-slot\">Ad</div></aside></div>\n<footer><p>Example News Ltd</p></footer>\n</body></html>\n"
}
